{"text": "saa\n\n\u2014\u2014\n\nwe\n\nBE\nate a 25 vmwany 3959\n\nMESA\neel\n\nI had spoken to you awhile back about our efforts in Mesa with the Landlord\nTraining Program. Right away, I want to tell you the more I am involved with\nthis program, the more I am impressed with what you have done, and all the work\nthat you do to keep it going.\n\nd\n\nDear John:\n\nYou may or may not be aware of the recent problems Tucson had with some people\nclaiming \u201cthe big, bad police\" were teaming up with the \"big, bad landlords\" to\npick on those who'were not financially well off, who had no CHOICE but to deal\ndrugs to supplement their incomes.\n\nYou might think this is hard to believe, but some group went to the city coun-\ncil down there and protested the program. The city council heeded their con-\ncerns and asked the police department to develop the program into a direction\nthat included tenant's rights.\n\nMesa is a community relations oriented city. When my supervisors saw the arti-\ncles, they were quite concerned. They were the main reason I worked toward the [i\ninformation I want to present to you. I would ask you to review the (color)\nhighlighted areas of the enclosed sheets of blue paper. I want you to see, I\nhave EVERY intention for crediting you for all of your excellent work. I don't\nwant to take anything away from you. Everytine I present a class, or give an\ninterview, I am committed to mentioning you and Campbell Resources. I am very\ngrateful for all you have done to help me with this progran.\n\nBecause we wanted to make the program look less geared toward \"landlords\" only.\nWe wanted to accentuate the benefits of your program that are geared toward\nthe tenants as well. (Such as C.P.T.E.D.)\n\nWe also included a \"block watch\" type training for the tenants as well to get\nthem on our side. We wanted to create a strong coalition between police, the\ntenants and management. In Arizona, \"landlord\" means \"slumlord\". It has a bad\nring to it. My lieutenant and sergeant specifically asked me to delete the\nword landlord.\n\nI'told them the program was CALLED The LANDLORD Training program, and I didn't\nhave the RIGHT to change it. I spoke to you briefly at the time, and I have\ntried to put this off as long as possible, but now I have to face it, and ask\nyou for your input.\n\nCurrently all of our books say \"Landlord Training Program\" just as the proofs\nI mailed to you awhile back. The new proposed cover for our 2nd edition would\nread: \"Crime Free Multi-Housing Prograi\n\nTHIS IS PENDING YOUR COMMENTS, by no means a done deal. I have alot of respect\nfor you Mr. Campbell, and I don't want to do ANYTHING that would give you some\nother opinion. The cover I included is a draft, I am open for your comments. I\nwill also submit them to my Lieutenant (who took your class in Portland about a\nyear or two ago).\n\nPolice Department\n1190 Nortn Robson Street + Mesa, Arizona 65201-6607 + (602) 644-2211",
